<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tisza Party</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Respect and Freedom Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> Party, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s second river and formally the Respect and Freedom Party, is a Hungarian centre-right political party. Founded in 2020, it was taken over in 2024 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-magyar">Péter Magyar</a>, a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidesz">Fidesz</a> insider, and rapidly became the main opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viktor-orban">Viktor Orbán</a>'s government. It sits with the European People's Party in the European Parliament.</p></div>
